 "findings": [
  {
   "severity": "medium",
   "title": "Rush mode soft-locks with an empty graveyard when hits come faster than ~20/s",
   "detail": "Each rush hit sets the zombie to 'bonk', which keeps its grave occupied for 0.32 s (index.html:636), then calls rushSpawn(1,g) (index.html:532). rushSpawn returns without spawning when no grave is empty (index.html:446), and nothing ever respawns later, because rush update (index.html:668) only updates zombies. So every failed spawn permanently removes one zombie from the 3-zombie chain. On a 3x3 grid this happens when the 7th hit lands within 0.32 s. Superhuman (1 tap per frame) scored 9 and then faced an empty field for 29.5 of the 30 s (fieldEmpty=1770 frames). world (~10 taps/s) scored 298 and was not affected. A human can't sustain the rate, but two-thumb bursts on 3x3 come close and the result is unrecoverable.",
   "repro": "cd qa/skill-tiers/push-zombie && PZRUNS='[[\"rush\",1]]' node bot.js superhuman  -> score 9, fieldEmpty 1770, firstEmpty 0.5 s",
   "fix": "Keep a pending-spawn counter: when rushSpawn finds no empty grave, increment it, and in update() spawn it as soon as a grave frees up. Alternatively, while stage-zombie count < 3, spawn on every frame that has a free grave."
  },
  {
   "severity": "medium",
   "title": "Timed mode: escape penalty wipes out low-tier scores",
   "detail": "Every escaped zombie costs -15 (index.html:631) while a normal hit gives +10. clumsy hit 36 zombies in 60 s and finished with score 0; casual hit 76 and scored 715, while skilled scored 2974 and world 4216. The lowest tier sees no reward for any success.",
   "repro": "PZRUNS='[[\"timed\",1]]' node bot.js clumsy  -> hits 36, score 0",
   "fix": "Lower the escape penalty (e.g. -5), or drop it during the first 15 s of timed mode."
  },
  {
   "severity": "low",
   "title": "Survival difficulty plateaus at ~166 s, so strong players never die",
   "detail": "diff()=gameTime/140 (index.html:403). Every params() field hits its clamp at d≈1.13-1.19 (index.html:407-411), so the game stops getting harder after ~166 s. skilled dies at 159-165 s (just before the plateau), while world and superhuman never lose a single heart in 300 s (3/3 runs each, capped). The survival run then only ends when the player gets bored. The curve is also steep below that: clumsy dies at 33-36 s, casual at 32-64 s.",
   "repro": "node bot.js world  -> survival end 'cap' 302 s, heartLoss []",
   "fix": "Keep a slow growth after the clamps (e.g. interval floor drops 1%/10 s, or add fast/helmet mix growth), so even world-level players eventually die (target ~4-6 min)."
  }
 ],
